Handlebars: Templates in tags using the Handlebars part type are now checked for syntax errors when they are saved. If a template contains a syntax error (e.g. an unclosed block), saving the page, template, object property or construct fails with "400 Bad Request" and an error message naming the tag, the part and the line, column and reason of the error. Unknown helpers and partials are not treated as errors, because they are only resolved when rendering.
